        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "\"In Problems 7–10, fit the data with the models given, using least squares.\"\n",
        "- The Textbook\n",
        "\n",
        "### Data\n",
        "\n",
        "| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n",
        "|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|:----|\n",
        "| $y$ | $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n",
        "\n",
        "### Models\n",
        "\n",
        "a. $y = b + ax$ \n",
        "\n",
        "a. $y = ax^2$\n",
        "\n",
        "### Solution\n",
        "1. First, we'll use the `numpy.polyfit()` method to \n",
        "produce least-squares optimized fits for each of the models given, because our models are already in polynomial form and that method already uses LS2 minimization to produce fitting functions.\n",
        "2. We'll use the `error_analyzer()` function from the `data_fitting.py` file (original work copyright 2026) to obtain the cumulative LS2 error. This file is available via [public github repo](https://github.com/GrandSlamVanDamme/math_283_U03_collab).\n",
        "\n",
        "3. We'll plot the original data against the lines of fit for a visual comparison."
      ],
      "id": "2d2655a6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        " # import the packages we need:\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from data_fitting import *\n",
        "\n",
        "# make our lists:\n",
        "\n",
        "X = np.array([1,2, 3, 4, 5])\n",
        "Y = np.array([1, 1, 2, 2, 5])\n",
        "\n",
        "#############################\n",
        "##  1. WRITE FUNCTIONS     ##\n",
        "#############################\n",
        "\n",
        "fit2 = np.polyfit(X, Y, 2)\n",
        "fit1 = np.polyfit(X, Y, 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "x = np.linspace(0, 6, 1000)\n",
        "\n",
        "f2 = fit2[0]*x**2 + fit2[1]*x**1 + fit2[2]*x**0\n",
        "f1 = fit1[0]*x**1 + fit1[1]*x**0 \n",
        "\n",
        "def get_coeffs(X, Y, n):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Takes the X and Y data, applies np.polyfit() for fit of chosen order n \n",
        "    and prints the elements neatly in form c_n = blahblahblah. \n",
        "    Each statement takes a line. Returns None.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    fit_list = np.polyfit(X, Y, n)\n",
        "\n",
        "    count = 0\n",
        "    cees = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for numba in fit_list:\n",
        "        count += 1\n",
        "        cees.append(f'c_{count}')\n",
        "    \n",
        "    for numba, c in zip(fit_list, cees):\n",
        "        print(f'{c}={numba}')\n",
        "\n",
        "#############################\n",
        "##   2. PLOTS              ##\n",
        "#############################\n",
        "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(10,5))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.subplot(1,2,1)\n",
        "plt.plot(x, f2)\n",
        "plt.scatter(X, Y)\n",
        "plt.title('$f(x)=c_1x^2+c_2x+c_3$')\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.subplot(1,2,2)\n",
        "plt.plot(x, f1)\n",
        "plt.scatter(X, Y)\n",
        "plt.title('$f(x)=c_1x+c_2$')\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "F1 = fit1[0]*X**1 + fit1[1]*X**0\n",
        "F2 = fit2[0]*X**2 + fit2[1]*X**1 + fit2[2]*X**0\n",
        "\n",
        "'''\n",
        "polyfit returns an array of n+1 entries \n",
        "each corresponding to the coefficient of\n",
        "x**n.\n",
        "'''"
      ],
      "id": "6255cb7d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Here are our results. \n",
        "\n",
        "First, let's look at the linear fit $f(x)=c_1x+c_2$."
